{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgfcxj5uY5b9HGL2Xkxf1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ruled F1 **DISMISS (not worth the cost)** and F2 **FIX**, and committed the verdict as 37d602cc9 (`docs/reviews/wi-963/013-ADJUDICATE-93526df.md`). The commit ends with `WI: WI-963` and `Loop-Session: 20261103T054112Z-32c0bd` in the same trailer block. The behaviour stays; what gets fixed is the text that overstates it.\n\n- **The behaviour is real.** Act A re-attests a row after its parent pointer was re-pointed. The pointer is then restored, and a later act B copies the same registry. The settlement filter then drops the row: it equals B's copy, and its routed cells are the same at both ends of the range.\n- **What actually goes unreported is narrow.**\n  - **The restore:** it's a traced change, and the snapshot already lets any act re-anchor traced pointers without a verdict. That's an existing kit rule, not this lane's.\n  - **The net diff:** across the range nothing routed moved, and the approved text change is exactly what A re-attested.\n- **Both remedies cost more than they buy.** Every hand landing is a single squash commit, so the re-attesting act's own copy can't be recovered there without changing the ledger format (IF-220).\n  - **F1's remedy (proof bound to that act)** therefore turns into minting every row a later act touches.\n  - **F2's remedy (delete the rule)** does the same directly.\n\n  Either way, the standard act turn would mint redundant rows again: an amendment act followed by a first-approval act on the same registry. WI-978's act would have re-minted TC-158, and the WI-926 replay that the lane's own completion criteria (Done-when item 6) require to mint nothing would mint all six rows.\n- **What is wrong is the text.** LLR-364 claims this rule proves \"nothing routed moved\", but it only proves equality at the range's two ends. Done-when item 5 (a row restored after its act still mints) reads as unbounded and collides with item 6. The fix:\n  - **The text:** state the rule's real limit in LLR-364, TC-403 and the RESYNC entry.\n  - **The test:** pin the restore-under-a-later-act case in TC-403 as settling.\n  - **Done-when item 5:** narrow it, through its in-lane blessing, to ranges with no later copy of the row's registry.\n\nI approved LLR-364 and TC-403 with this rule at sittings 008 and 009, and the verdict says so. The rule itself was the coordinator's call (D-014), so the owner can still overrule it on review if they'd rather have the redundant rows.\n\nThe commit hooks passed, but again reported that the `format` check didn't run (ruff isn't installed). I committed only the verdict, so `013-ADJUDICATE-93526df.md.requested` is still untracked."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":685,"cache_read_input_tokens":720622,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":685},"output_tokens":729,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f031c6a5-ecf0-490f-9890-c7a8a87f92fc","uuid":"f7d506df-ed01-4335-be88-d24279cfa936","timestamp":"2026-11-03T07:44:12.984Z","request_id":"req_011CgfcxinJsJAikhFFVVePC"}
